  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.632 acc. All completed multimodal experiments used resnet50 as the image encoder; imagenet_vit_l has never been tested. Image-only performance is low (0.208), but in the multimodal setting the image modality adds ~0.03-0.04 over RNA-only, and it is unclear whether a stronger, larger image encoder (ViT-L) could extract more complementary signal. Question: config_036 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) while holding all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, concat), cleanly isolating the image-encoder effect. Why this is the best next experiment: It resolves a major untested design dimension with a single-variable comparison to the current best. If ViT-L improves performance, it signals the image modality is underutilized and further image-side investment is warranted; if it does not, it confirms resnet50 is sufficient and redirects budget toward RNA-encoder or fusion choices. This is higher-information than testing weighted fusion (nearly resolved by singleprofile evidence) or transformer aggregation (already shown inferior to avgpool)."
}

